course: dictionary
lesson: 15657
title: Thereto in formal writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound old-fashioned because they belong to formal writing, such as contracts, rules and legal documents. «Thereto» is one of them. The word is made of «there» and «to», and it means «to that» or «to it», pointing back to something already mentioned. «The club rules, and any changes thereto, are on the notice board.» Here «thereto» points back to the rules: the changes to the rules are on the board.
explain: You can often swap the word for a simpler one to check. Try «to it» or «to that» in the sentence. «We agreed thereto, so the deal was signed.» If you swap in «we agreed to that», the sentence still makes sense, so thereto must mean to that.
explain: You will hardly ever hear thereto in a playground or at home. People say «to it» instead. Thereto belongs to formal writing, where precise words matter, so you are most likely to meet it in a contract, a form or an exam question.
fact: Thereto means «to that» or «to it», referring back to something already mentioned.
fact: Thereto is an adverb, and it is formal, so it is found mostly in legal documents and contracts.
fact: In everyday speech, people say «to it» instead of thereto.
fact: Common phrases with thereto include «attached thereto», «changes thereto» and «agreed thereto».
exercise: «The school rules, and any changes thereto, are on the wall.» What does thereto mean here? | Far away from the school | Instead of lunch | Because it was raining | *To the rules
exercise: «We agreed thereto, so the deal was signed.» What does thereto mean? | *To that agreement | With a red pen | Before the sun rose | Very quickly
exercise: «The form was attached thereto, so keep both papers together.» Find and copy the word that means «to it». | papers | together | *thereto | form
test: «Sign the contract and any terms attached thereto.» Where are the terms? | *Attached to the contract | Read aloud at lunch | Hidden in the playground | Lost under the desk
test: What is the everyday swap for thereto in «the changes thereto»? | *the changes to it | the changes under the table | the changes before lunch | the changes for ever
exam: Which sentence uses thereto correctly? | «We went thereto for lunch and ate pizza.» | «She bought thereto a new red bike.» | «Thereto the dog barked loudly at the postman.» | *«The rules, and all amendments thereto, must be read carefully.»
